      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subject offered: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- Mathematics department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- Course 18: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- degree-granting department: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- department name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- subject title: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- school name: STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME\n- department code: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- average number of enrolled students: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"Mathematics\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '18'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. List the department name, subject title, number of enrolled students, and school name for each subject offered, along with dense ranks over the department code ordered by department code, for subjects with more than 0 enrolled students in departments that grant degrees, specifically for the Mathematics department (Course 18).\n```sql\nSELECT t0.DEPARTMENT_NAME, t1.SUBJECT_TITLE, t1.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, t2.SCHOOL_NAME, DENSE_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE ORDER BY t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE) AS window_column FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT t0 JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t1 ON t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t1.OFFER_DEPT_CODE JOIN STUDENT_DEPARTMENT t2 ON t1.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = t2.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE t1.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0 AND t0.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND t0.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics' AND t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '18'\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each subject offered in the Mathematics department (Course 18) that has more than 0 enrolled students and is in a degree-granting department, list the department name, subject title, number of enrolled students, and school name, along with a dense rank over the department code ordered by department code, but only include those subjects where the number of enrolled students is greater than the average number of enrolled students for all subjects in the Mathematics department. Do not return any rounded answers."
