      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 77, \"items_by_type\": {\"table\": [{\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Section-level subject offering fact table: one row per subject section offered in a term, with section flags (master/lecture/lab/recitation/design), cluster information, offering department and school, responsible faculty, meeting time/place, and enrollment numbers at section, subject, and cluster level. Linked to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject level) via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY/COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY and to SUBJECT_SUMMARY via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Library subject offered table: subjects offered per term that appear in library reserve processing, with subject identity, course number, offering department/school, responsible faculty, and enrollment count. Parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with department/school attribution, unit structure (total/lecture/lab/prep/design units), and detailed enrollment statistics including final enrollment, first-week and fifth-week enrollment, and credit/listener splits at both subject and cluster level. Used for enrollment and unit statistics by department, school, term, and subject group.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"Student-facing department lookup table with department code, name, full name, and school attribution (code and name). Similar in content to SIS_DEPARTMENT but oriented to student information systems reporting; joins to offering tables via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) subject offered table: one row per subject offered in a term within the textbook program scope, with subject identity, offering department/school, responsible faculty, enrollment count, and a flag indicating whether the subject has no course material. Parent of TIP_DETAIL via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\", \"desc\": \"SIS subject code lookup table mapping subject codes and course numbers to their descriptions, departments, and schools. Used to resolve subject code descriptions and to link courses to departments via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Student directory table: one row per student with name components, full name, office location and phone, email address, department code and department name, and student year. The DEPARTMENT column stores the academic department code and joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, enabling per-department student counts.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_ENROLLABLE\", \"desc\": \"11 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"CIS course catalog table: an alternative course catalog source with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags), keyed by academic year, term code, and subject identity. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via DEPARTMENT_CODE for subject code resolution.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"desc\": \"SIS course description table: catalog descriptions of courses with department and school attribution, course level (undergraduate/graduate), degree-granting flag, graduate level, CIP program code, and effective from/thru terms. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEGREE_PROGRAM\", \"desc\": \"19 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE\", \"desc\": \"Subject attribute lookup table decoding attribute codes attached to subjects: academic attributes (type 'A') such as calculus/science prerequisites and HASS-D/HASS category codes, and non-academic program flags (type 'N') such as ROTC, ESG, Concourse, co-op, and listener rules. Provides short, full, and reporting descriptions per code. Overlaps with CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE on HASS-family codes (HD1-HD5, HDL, HE, HA, HH, HS) but differs in scope: SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE covers all subject attribute types with one description variant per code, while CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE covers only HASS attribute codes with separate registration-form and bulletin descriptions plus attribute-group (H/G) classification. Catalog subject records' GIR_ATTRIBUTE codes all resolve against SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"Drupal-sourced course catalog table: an alternative catalog feed with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags, section flags, meeting time/place), plus subject-offering reference columns (SO_SUBJECT_ID, SO_TERM_CODE, SO_TERM_DESCRIPTION, SO_CLUSTER_TYPE) linking catalog records to registrar subject offerings.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject category lookup table with category name and description. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Employee directory table: one row per institute employee with MIT ID, legal and preferred name components, directory/primary titles, HR department number and name, office location and office phone, email address, personal URL, and Kerberos name. Used to resolve responsible faculty contact details (full name, email, office phone) for subject offerings via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID, and to link employees to Moira mailing list membership via MIT_ID = MOIRA_LIST_MEMBER_MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_IAP_SCHEDULE\", \"desc\": \"10 columns in total\"}], \"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_50\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects offered in 2021 that are not for graduate credit, are listed as undergraduate in the course catalog, are in the Mathematics department, and are also offered by the School of Science? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2210\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code in degree-granting departments where the department is Mathematics, and for subjects offered in the academic year 2024 that are also present in the CIS course catalog and are in the Mathematics department, show the subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, rank of the subject code within each school name group ordered by subject code, subject ID, subject number, subject short title, subject title, lecture units, lab units, total units, grade type, grade rule, the minimum total units value over each department code group, and the subject description from the CIS course catalog, ordered by school name, rank, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4658\", \"desc\": \"Show the Mathematics department courses with at least 5 enrolled students, including the course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, the row number within each academic year group ordered by course number, the term start date, calendar date, day of week, the average calendar year within each calendar year group ordered by term start date, and for each course, also display the responsible faculty name and the offer school name, but only for academic terms where the term status is 'Previous'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3248\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units that are also offered in the library by the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code, the number of enrolled students, offering department name, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1758\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with total units equal to 12 in the Mathematics department, show the department code, department name, subject code, subject number, subject title, total units, the row number within each department ordered by subject code, the deviation of each subject's total units from the average total units of all Mathematics subjects offered in 2024, the number of enrolled students, responsible faculty name, school name, and the dense rank over the department name ordered by department name for those subjects that also have course materials and were offered in the term '2019FA'. Sort the table by department name and subject title. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4229\", \"desc\": \"For IAP subjects in the \\\"Mathematics\\\" category, show the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, activity description, and the row number within each enrollment type group ordered by activity title, along with the academic year, department name, average enrollment, enrollment variance, department phone number, and school name for each academic year and department where the IAP subject's term matches a department's fall term subject offering with more than 0 enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2365\", \"desc\": \"For the top 3 most frequently offered courses in the Mathematics department, for each course and each term it was offered, display the course number, course description, subject title, number of times offered, department name, number of unique course descriptions for that course and department, the minimum CIP program code for that course and department, the term code, the term description, the school name, and the department phone number. Do not repeat the course number if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by course number and term code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1350\", \"desc\": \"For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, and the total enrolled students, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with at least one enrolled student. Additionally, for each school, include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, nulls for statistics, and total enrolled students). For students whose first name is 'Peter' and who are in the Mathematics department, also show their last name, email address, student year, and the minimum department budget code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's full name, as well as the department full name and department last activity date. The results include all these columns in the following order: department name, school name, average enrolled students, range of enrolled students, variance of enrolled students, total enrolled students, last name, email address, student year, windowed minimum department budget code, department full name, and department last activity date. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2090\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units in the Mathematics department, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, and the rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code, along with the department name, school name, the highest number of degree-granting undergraduate courses in the Mathematics department (Course 18), and the subject short title and subject description for each subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4724\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the library in the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Additionally, for the corresponding offering department and school, provide the number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ' and the minimum total units for those subjects. Also, include the department phone number and the school name for the offering department, and display the responsible faculty name for each subject. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, maximum total units for each row and the next two rows, number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ', minimum total units for those subjects, department phone number, school name, and responsible faculty name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3632\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", show the subject title, subject key, offer department name, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, subject ID, academic year, term description, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row, ordered by offer department name and academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1212\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department (Course 18), provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student), the number of graduate students in the department, and the most recent warehouse load date for those students, considering only departments that are degree granting and students whose year is 'G'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_5150\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects in the course catalog are offered in the spring term, have a total of at least 6 units, are taught by faculty who are responsible for at least one subject with more than 0 enrolled students according to the subject offered summary, and are in the Mathematics department (Course 18)? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4584\", \"desc\": \"For Mathematics department courses with at least 5 enrolled students, show the course number, subject title, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, the row number within each academic year group ordered by course number, the term start date, calendar date, day of week, and the average calendar year within each calendar year group ordered by term start date, but only for academic terms where the term status is 'Previous', and only include results where the number of enrolled students is greater than the average number of enrolled students for that academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3237\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of active graduate students with an office location assigned in that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4527\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with a non-null subject code description), and, for each subject in 2021 offered by these departments in the School of Engineering, list the subject id, subject title, and the number of enrolled students, but only include subjects where the number of enrolled students exceeds the average enrollment for that department in 2021. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1766\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting, the total units are greater than 6, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the department name, course level, number of unique courses, minimum total units offered, school name, number of distinct course options available, and the highest average number of enrolled students in any term for courses offered by that department, considering only courses with more than 0 enrolled students and departments whose name is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3215\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2012, show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, academic year, term description, the row number within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, the subject code, subject code description, department name, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the school code and ordered by school code, for subjects where the school code is not null and the subject title is not null. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1427\", \"desc\": \"For each course in the Mathematics department that is degree granting and has a course level of 'G', show the course description, department name, school name, the administrative department name, and the dense rank over the administrative department name ordered by the administrative department name. Additionally, for each administrative department name, include a grand total of the number of such courses in the format of (null, null, null, administrative department name, null, total courses). Also, show the minimum total units, the sum of lecture units, and the number of unique subjects for letter graded Mathematics department subjects offered in the Spring Term 2021, along with the department name and term description (with all other columns as null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}], \"concept\": [{\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_person_directory\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing people of the institute keyed by MIT_ID: the primary employee directory (contact details, titles, HR department), the Drupal-sourced employee feed (employee group/type, appointment flags, HR org unit), the person master table (payroll rank, position title, active flag), the HR faculty roster (appointment type, terminal degree, emeritus status), the OPA current-person snapshot (HR job/appointment attributes, faculty flag, sabbatical), and the student directory (students with department attribution and student year). They jointly answer questions about who a person is, their contact details, job/appointment attributes, and whether they are employee, faculty, or student; responsible faculty in subject offering tables resolve to these tables via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_catalog_sources\", \"desc\": \"Tables providing catalog-level subject attributes (titles, unit structure, grading rules, HGN level, requirement attributes, offering-term flags) from different source systems: the warehouse course catalog, the CIS course catalog feed, and the Drupal course catalog feed. They answer the same catalog-attribute questions but differ in source system, extra columns, and join paths to department/subject-code lookups.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_academic_term_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing academic terms and their calendar/status attributes. They jointly answer questions about when terms run, which academic/financial-aid/degree year a term belongs to, and whether a term is current, previous, future, or regular. Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_iap_activities\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing Independent Activities Period (IAP) activities offered in January terms: activity details (title, enrollment type, max enrollment, fee, cancellation flags), sessions (location, date, times), sponsors (name, type), categories, and persons. They jointly answer questions about IAP activity counts, enrollment capacity, fees, session scheduling, and sponsorship.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_moira_mailing_lists\", \"desc\": \"Tables of the Moira mailing-list/group domain: the list master (one row per list with name, description, active flag, and type flags such as mailing list, group, NFS group, public, hidden), the membership detail (one row per list member with member login, full name, MIT ID, and last update date), and the owner lookup (one row per owner entity with owner name and owner type LIST/USER/KERBEROS). They jointly answer questions about which lists exist and their properties, who belongs to a list, and who owns a list; MOIRA_LIST is the parent of MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_KEY, and MOIRA_LIST_OWNER is referenced by MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_OWNER_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical building inventory and its attributes (number/name, type, ownership, site, campus sector, access level, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates): the current FCLT_* family snapshot, its fiscal-period history (in two date-format variants), the FAC_* family snapshot, and the lightweight space-domain building lookup. They jointly answer questions about building characteristics, areas, and room counts, but differ in time coverage, table family, attribute richness, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_time_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Time dimension tables of the warehouse at three granularities: TIME_DAY (one row per calendar date, with fiscal/calendar year and period, academic year, financial aid year, day of week, and the academic term code/description of the day), TIME_MONTH (one row per fiscal period in YYYYMM format, covering fiscal years 1996-2035, with fiscal quarter, calendar month, academic term, and financial aid year mappings), and TIME_QUARTER (one row per fiscal quarter, covering fiscal years 2000-2035, with quarter dates, payroll certification deadlines, and quarter status flags). They jointly answer questions about when fiscal periods/quarters/days run, which fiscal/calendar/academic year a date or month belongs to, and how day-level records roll up to months and quarters. They link to each other via FISCAL_PERIOD (day-month), FY_QUARTER_CODE (month-quarter), and FISCAL_YEAR (month-quarter association within the same fiscal year, fanning out months across all quarters of the year), and to the academic term tables via TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE or TIME_MONTH.ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_major_use_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables classifying rooms by major use (classrooms, offices, laboratories, residential, circulation, etc.) with a short code, description, and assignable-space flag. They cover the current classification in the FCLT and FAC table families and the fiscal-period historical classification in the FCLT family, jointly answering questions about what a room is primarily used for and whether that use counts as assignable space.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_cip_program_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables of the Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) used to classify courses/instructional programs into two-digit categories, four-digit series, and six-digit program codes, with revision version years (1990/2000/2010/2020). CIP holds the current single-version classification (one row per program code, with a change NOTE), while CIP_WITH_VERSION preserves every revision of each program code across versions. Both join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs and categories.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_facility_organization_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Organization dimension tables describing the institute's hierarchical organization tree used for facilities/space attribution: FCLT_ORGANIZATION (keyed by FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, with DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME) and FAC_ORGANIZATION (keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY, with D_CODE). They answer the same questions about organization names, hierarchy levels, parent/major organizations, assignable flags, and HR cross-references, but belong to different table families and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_space_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical room inventory and its space assignment: SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to space units with usage classification and square footage), FCLT_ROOMS (facilities room inventory with use classifications, organization assignment, and area in square meters), FAC_ROOMS (the FAC_* family room snapshot with the same structure as FCLT_ROOMS but FAC_* keys), and ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (space-planning room load feed with floor, space usage text, access level, and space unit code / HR org unit id links). They jointly answer questions about how many rooms exist, room sizes, room usage, and which organization/space unit occupies rooms, but differ in assignment perspective, key family, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_floor_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the floor level of buildings: the current FCLT_* family floor inventory with floor areas, the FAC_* family floor snapshot with the same structure, the fiscal-period historical floor table, and the lightweight space-domain floor lookup. They jointly answer questions about floor numbers and per-floor assignable/non-assignable areas, but differ in time coverage, table family, and attribute richness.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_space_unit_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Space unit lookup tables identifying the organizational units that receive space allocation: SPACE_UNIT (with FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution) and SPACE_UNIT2 (identity/name only). They answer the same space-unit identity questions but differ in organization linkage and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_address\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the postal/street addresses of buildings: the current FCLT_* family address table (multiple purpose-typed address rows per building), its fiscal-period historical counterpart, the FAC_* family address snapshot, and the single-text address fields of the space-domain BUILDINGS lookup. They jointly answer questions about where a building is located (street number/name, city, state, postal code), but differ in time coverage, address decomposition, and table family.\"}], \"column_concept\": [{\"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_office_location\", \"desc\": \"OFFICE_LOCATION columns recording where a person's office/desk is, replicated across the person-directory tables (SE_PERSON, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY). All hold a building or building-room text identifier in the same value domain as FCLT_ROOMS.BUILDING_ROOM, but they describe different populations (employee/person master vs student vs primary employee directory vs Drupal employee feed) and differ sharply in non-null coverage and in how many values are building-room ('BLDG-ROOM') versus building-only ('BLDG'). Choosing the right column determines whose office is reported and whether room-level joins to FCLT_ROOMS succeed.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_hass_attribute\", \"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code and description columns. The code columns appear in the three course catalog feeds and in the CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE lookup; description columns exist in three variants: the catalog-embedded HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC, the lookup's DESCRIPTION_ON_FORM (registration-form wording), and DESCRIPTION_IN_BULLETIN (short bulletin wording). Selecting the right description variant depends on the wording requested by the question.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_type_site\", \"desc\": \"Building classification columns replicated across the current and historical building tables of both table families: BUILDING_TYPE ('ACADEMIC', 'SERVICE', 'RESIDENT') and SITE ('MIT', 'BATES', 'LINC', 'BOS', etc.). They carry the same value domain but differ in time semantics: the building-table columns are the current classification, while the history-table columns are the classification recorded at each fiscal period, so filtering by one versus the other can select different building sets.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_year_columns\", \"desc\": \"Year columns across term, catalog, and time dimension tables representing different year systems: academic year, fiscal year, financial aid year, and degree year. Selecting the correct year system is essential for yearly grouping and partitioning.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_material_status_key\", \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_num_of_rooms\", \"desc\": \"NUM_OF_ROOMS columns recording how many rooms a building contains, replicated across the current and historical building tables of both families. The building-table columns hold the current room count (one value per building); the history-table columns hold the room count at each fiscal period, used for room-count statistics (average, range, variance, minimum) across a building's history records.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_assignable_area\", \"desc\": \"Assignable-area measure columns at different granularity levels and time semantics: building-level current and per-fiscal-period assignable area, floor-level assignable area, and the space-domain assignable square footage. All FCLT_*/FAC_* columns are in square meters; BUILDINGS.BLDG_ASSIGNABLE_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet. Choosing the right column determines whether the measure is a building total, a floor total, a historical value, or a space-assignment figure.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_room\", \"desc\": \"Combined building-room identifier columns (e.g. '1-080') appearing in both the space assignment fact table and the facilities room inventory. They identify the same physical room concept but come from different business processes with different coverage and companion measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_access_level\", \"desc\": \"Access level columns recorded at three granularity levels of the facilities domain plus the space-planning room feed: building-level ACCESS_LEVEL_CODE/ACCESS_LEVEL_NAME (current and per-fiscal-period history), floor-level ACCESS_LEVEL, and room-level ACCESS_LEVEL (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD). They share a numeric value domain (observed 0-3) but describe the access restriction of different physical objects or come from different feeds, so filters and joins must target the granularity and table family the question refers to.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_fiscal_period\", \"desc\": \"Fiscal period code columns in YYYYMM format (e.g. '199602' = FY1996 period 2, '201505') appearing in two distinct roles: as the primary key of the month-grain time dimension (TIME_MONTH.FISCAL_PERIOD, also mirrored in TIME_DAY.FISCAL_PERIOD for day-to-month linkage), and as the snapshot-period stamp of the facilities historical tables (FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST, FCLT_FLOOR_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST). Both roles share the same YYYYMM value domain, but the time dimension uses it for calendar grouping while the history tables use it to mark when a facilities snapshot was taken.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_facility_organization_key\", \"desc\": \"Facility organization key columns attributing space units and rooms to organizations in the hierarchical organization tree. Two naming conventions exist across table families (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY in FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables vs ORGANIZATION_KEY in FAC_* tables) with the same value domain.\"}]}}"
    },
